Carafe bench: the shader recompiler translates IMUL, IMUL32I and PRMT. NAK, the compiler of NVK,
emits them for Maxwell (integer multiplies and byte extracts), NVN never does, and Eden threw
"Instruction IMUL (imm)/PRMT (imm) is not implemented", built no pipeline and skipped every draw
that used it. DXVK's Direct3D 9 fixed-function shaders contain both, so a D3D9 game drew nothing.
IMUL.HI is built from 16-bit partial products so every backend runs it without 64-bit integers.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

